DELETE and MERGE INTO statements only\");","+\t\t\tthrow NotImplementedException(\"EXPLAIN (SQL) supports SELECT, VALUES, WITH, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, \"","+\t\t\t                              \"MERGE INTO, CREATE TABLE ... AS and COPY ... TO statements only\");"," \t\t}"," \t}"," "],"additions":13,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/planner/operator/logical_explain.cpp","lines":["@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@ unique_ptr<LogicalOperator> LogicalExplain::CreateSQLResult(ClientContext &conte"," \tcase LogicalOperatorType::LOGICAL_UPDATE:"," \tcase LogicalOperatorType::LOGICAL_DELETE:"," \tcase LogicalOperatorType::LOGICAL_MERGE_INTO:","+\tcase LogicalOperatorType::LOGICAL_CREATE_TABLE:","+\tcase LogicalOperatorType::LOGICAL_COPY_TO_FILE:"," \t\t// a data-modifying statement reports a change count; that is not a projection of the generated SQL"," \t\tbreak;"," \tdefault:"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/planner/sql_export/CMakeLists.txt","lines":["@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ add_library_unity(","   sql_export_relations.cpp","   sql_export_scope.cpp","   sql_export_sources.cpp","+  sql_export_statements.cpp","   sql_export_values.cpp","   sql_export_window.cpp","   table_function_sql_export.cpp)"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/planner/sql_export/README.md","lines":["@@ -22,9 +22,9 @@ Optimization can also fold observations made while planning into the generated S"," "," ## Supported statements and errors"," ","-SQL mode accepts supported SELECT, VALUES, and WITH queries, and INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, and MERGE INTO statements. It does not combine with ANALYZE or FORMAT, and it does not support DDL, CALL, or EXPLAIN EXECUTE. Existing restrictions on SQL PREPARE also apply. Some logical operators and expressions cannot yet be exported; their errors describe the unsupported query or source. The C++ export result retains structured issue codes, phases, and plan locations. Unsupported export never returns the original query as a fallback.","+SQL mode accepts supported SELECT, VALUES, and WITH queries, and INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, MERGE INTO, CREATE TABLE ... AS, and COPY ... TO statements. It does not combine with ANALYZE or FORMAT, and it does not support other DDL, CALL, or EXPLAIN EXECUTE. Existing restrictions on SQL PREPARE also apply. Some logical operators and expressions cannot yet be exported; their errors describe the unsupported query or source. The C++ export result retains structured issue codes, phases, and plan locations. Unsupported export never returns the original query as a fallback."," ","-An exported data-modifying statement reconstructs its bound source as a query: an INSERT becomes `INSERT INTO` the table's physical columns from a generated query, and UPDATE and DELETE statements key the modified rows by the table's `rowid` column computed in a generated subquery. A MERGE INTO exports its bound source join as the USING relation, keyed back to the target by row id, with each bound action reconstructed; `ON CONFLICT` inserts export through their MERGE INTO binding. `RETURNING` lists are reconstructed against the modified table's columns, and data-modifying CTEs export as materialized CTE bodies, both as producers and with a data-modifying statement as the consumer. `WHEN NOT MATCHED BY SOURCE` actions, triggers on the modified table, and tables without a single named row-id column are rejected.","+An exported data-modifying statement reconstructs its bound source as a query: an INSERT becomes `INSERT INTO` the table's physical columns from a generated query, and UPDATE and DELETE statements key the modified rows by the table's `rowid` column computed in a generated subquery. A CREATE TABLE ... AS or COPY ... TO exports its bound source as a query carrying the created or written column names. The COPY sink options re-emit from the operator's resolved state, including PARTITION_BY, ordering, overwrite and rotation settings, while format-specific options stay as bound. A computed file path, PARTITION_PATH, and orderings that are not plain written columns are rejected. A MERGE INTO exports its bound source join as the USING relation, keyed back to the target by row id, with each bound action reconstructed; `ON CONFLICT` inserts export through their MERGE INTO binding. `RETURNING` lists are reconstructed against the modified table's columns, and data-modifying CTEs export as materialized CTE bodies, both as producers and with a data-modifying statement as the consumer. `WHEN NOT MATCHED BY SOURCE` actions, triggers on the modified table, and tables without a single named row-id column are rejected."," "," PIVOT with values discovered from data is rejected because column discovery requires executing auxiliary statements. Specify the values with an explicit IN list to export supported PIVOT queries. Unresolved parameters and explicit optimizer opt-outs may also leave unsupported plan nodes."," "],"additions":2,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/planner/sql_export/logical_plan_sql_exporter.cpp","lines":["@@ -95,8 +95,8 @@ static LogicalPlanSQLExportResult EnsureSQLProjection(LogicalPlanSQLExportResult"," \treturn result;"," }"," ","-static LogicalPlanSQLExportResult ApplyOutputNames(LogicalPlanSQLExportResult result,","-                                                   const vector<Identifier> &output_names) {","+LogicalPlanSQLExportResult LogicalPlanSQLExportHelpers::ApplyOutputNames(LogicalPlanSQLExportResult result,","+                                                                         const vector<Identifier> &output_names) {"," \tif (result.HasError()) {"," \t\treturn result;"," \t}","@@ -264,6 +264,34 @@ LogicalPlanSQLExportContext::ExportChild(LogicalOperator &child, const LogicalPl"," \treturn ExportChild(child, path);"," }"," ","+LogicalPlanVerificationResult<LogicalPlanSQLExportedChild>","+LogicalPlanSQLExportContext::ExportRoot(LogicalOperator &root, const LogicalPlanVerificationPath &path,","+                  